explanation:
`filter` keeps elements for which the closure returns `true`, `map` turns each expense into its title, and `reduce(0)` folds every amount into one total. `sorted` puts `$0` first whenever the closure returns `true`, so `$0.amount > $1.amount` gives descending order; `<` would put the cheapest first.

```swift
let large = expenses.filter { $0.amount > 50 }
let titles = large.map { $0.title }
let spent = expenses.reduce(0) { $0 + $1.amount }
let biggestFirst = expenses.sorted { $0.amount > $1.amount }
```
